 "intro_zh": "青城山景区位于四川省成都市都江堰市西南，是中国首批公布的风景名胜区之一。青城山靠岷山雪岭，面向川西平原，群峰环绕，状若城廓；林深树密，四季常绿；丹梯千级，曲径通幽。都江堰不仅是举世闻名的中国古代水利工程，也是著名的风景名胜区。都江堰附近景色秀丽，文物古迹众多，主要有伏龙观、二王庙、安澜索桥、玉垒关、离堆公园、玉垒山公园、玉女峰、灵岩寺、普照寺、翠月湖、都江堰水利工程等。",
 "intro_en": "Mount Qingcheng (Chinese: 青城山; pinyin: Qīngchéng Shān) is a sacred Taoist mountain in Dujiangyan, Chengdu, Sichuan, China. It is considered one of the birthplaces of Taoism and one of the most important Taoist religious sites in China. In Taoist mythology, it was the site of the Yellow Emperor's studies with Ning Fengzi. As an important site of the Taoism, it became host to many Taoist monasteries and temples. The mountain has 36 peaks. It is also home to Dujiangyan Giant Panda Center and since 2000 has been listed as a UNESCO World Heritage Site. Mount Qingcheng was affected by the Wenchuan Earthquake in 2008.",
 "intro_en_source": "wikipedia",
